    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 48\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 1724, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  civil service law, in relation to employee\n      representation of state employees designated managerial or  confi-\n      dential\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would extend to organizations that advocate for managerial\nor confidential employees the right to certain employee information  and\nprocesses currently required for union represented employees.\n \n  As noted in my previous veto of this bill, this proposal would improp-\nerly  extend  to any voluntary group advocating for managerial or confi-\ndential employees the same statutory rights afforded  to  union  repres-\nented employees, despite having no statutory or contractual relationship\nwith  those  employees.  It  is also duplicative of existing methods for\ncontacting this class of employees to inform  such  employees  of  their\nservices and resources.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 48,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
